1
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:05,980
=The Cruel Tribunal=
=Episode 3=

2
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:07,360
The person I'm here to sue today

3
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,760
is you, Official Huang.

4
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,080
Today,

5
00:01:11,090 --> 00:01:13,150
I'm here on behalf of the people
of the Eastern Market.

6
00:01:13,160 --> 00:01:14,720
I'm sure you already know

7
00:01:14,730 --> 00:01:17,580
about the forced demolition
of the Eastern Market for the Imperial Retreat.

8
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:23,400
How did we end up as the defendants?

9
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:24,560
But

10
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:27,200
the Eastern Market
does fall under our jurisdiction.

11
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:28,840
Then...

12
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:29,760
Why don't we

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,280
hear what she has to say first?

14
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:34,040
The decision came from above anyway.

15
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:35,260
It has nothing to do with you.

16
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:39,880
Advocate Jiang,

17
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:40,880
I do know

18
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:42,480
a little about the matter.

19
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,920
Since you're already aware of it,

20
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:45,080
you should know

21
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:46,510
that forcibly demolishing
the Eastern Market

22
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:47,700
harms the people's interests,

23
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:48,950
undermines their trust
in the authorities,

24
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:50,680
and violates the principles of law.

25
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,320
From a legal standpoint,

26
00:01:53,330 --> 00:01:54,630
the forced demolition
of the Eastern Market

27
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:56,080
violates due process.

28
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:59,160
Protecting people's property
is fundamental to the state.

29
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:02,080
If you're demolishing the Eastern Market
for the Imperial Retreat,

30
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:04,440
have the merchants
been fairly compensated?

31
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,520
Have you consulted
the people on the plan?

32
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:08,680
Building the Imperial Retreat
may be a good thing,

33
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:10,630
but you can't leave so many merchants
without a livelihood.

34
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:11,950
If you demolish it
just because you say so,

35
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,280
how can they ever trust you again?

36
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,440
- Exactly!
- Exactly!

37
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:16,300
- How can we trust you?
- How can we trust you?

38
00:02:17,430 --> 00:02:19,480
How many people
depend on this market for a living?

39
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:21,000
If it's forcibly demolished,

40
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,230
how are they supposed to survive?

41
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,000
- Exactly!
- Exactly!

42
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,620
- How are we supposed to survive?
- How are we supposed to survive?

43
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:26,440
More importantly,

44
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:27,720
when the market thrives,

45
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:29,280
the city prospers.

46
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:30,320
But

47
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,000
if the people become disillusioned,

48
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,780
then when the government
needs to collect grain and taxes

49
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:35,510
or recruit soldiers,

50
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,880
who will willingly comply?

51
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:38,160
As the old saying goes,

52
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:39,440
water can carry a boat,

53
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:40,600
but it can also overturn it.

54
00:02:40,610 --> 00:02:42,040
The Imperial Retreat is being built

55
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,640
so His Majesty can rest and recuperate.

56
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:44,880
The people need the market

57
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:46,790
to earn a living
and support their families.

58
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:47,920
So weigh the two.

59
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:49,080
Which matters more?

60
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:50,680
Official Huang.

61
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,850
The First Prince is waiting
for you in the rear hall.

62
00:02:58,880 --> 00:02:59,680
Your Highness.

63
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:00,560
I apologize

64
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,760
for not welcoming you sooner.

65
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:05,040
No need for such formalities,
Official Huang.

66
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:06,280
Thank you, Your Highness.

67
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:07,480
I just heard

68
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:09,690
that you're hearing
the Eastern Market demolition case.

69
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:10,520
Yes, indeed.

70
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:11,200
I've

71
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:12,960
been quite troubled by this matter.

72
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,480
Why is it so difficult?

73
00:03:14,800 --> 00:03:15,880
Your Highness may not know,

74
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,760
but the Yushan Imperial Retreat project

75
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,960
is personally overseen by Prince Luan.

76
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:21,120
Now

77
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:22,800
the people have raised objections,

78
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:25,600
and I'm truly caught in the middle.

79
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:26,760
I believe

80
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:28,920
the people must always come first.

81
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:30,990
Understand their hardships
and ease their burdens.

82
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:34,000
Putting the people's interests first

83
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,440
is the duty of an official.

84
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:37,160
But

85
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,440
what if Prince Luan...

86
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,920
Do what you believe is right.

87
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,080
Don't worry.

88
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,440
If Prince Luan takes issue with it,

89
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:45,280
I'll handle it.

90
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,840
I understand.

91
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:55,920
After

92
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,320
careful consideration,

93
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,500
I have decided to grant

94
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:00,280
the Eastern Market merchants' request

95
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:01,240
and temporarily suspend

96
00:04:01,250 --> 00:04:02,680
the demolition of the Eastern Market.

97
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:03,860
I will report this to my superiors

98
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:04,600
and recommend

99
00:04:04,610 --> 00:04:05,980
that the road to the Imperial Retreat

100
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:07,360
be rerouted.

101
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,040
Your Honor.

102
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,080
Say no more.

103
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:10,080
I believe

104
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:10,880
the people

105
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,240
must always come first.

106
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,440
Understand their hardships

107
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:14,440
(Bright Mirror Hangs High)
and ease their burdens.

108
00:04:14,450 --> 00:04:15,640
Putting the people's interests

109
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:16,640
first

110
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,920
is the duty of an official.

111
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:18,920
This case

112
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:20,240
is closed.

113
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:22,280
Court dismissed.

114
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,520
Yes!

115
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:28,840
- Thank you, Your Honor!
- Thank you, Your Honor!

116
00:04:29,520 --> 00:04:30,480
Let's go!

117
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:32,480
Wonderful!

118
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:54,140
(Guaranteed Win)

119
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,000
Xiaobai.

120
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:58,120
I bought your favorite pastries.

121
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:01,800
Take your money back.

122
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:03,880
What do you mean?

123
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:05,840
Xiaobai,

124
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,000
isn't this money

125
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:08,920
the legal fee the people paid you?

126
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:10,800
What ordinary person

127
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,200
could afford such
an exquisite silk purse?

128
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:16,520
So you knew all along.

129
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,240
Then if you knew

130
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:19,890
the people
couldn't afford the legal fee,

131
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,600
why did you still take their case?

132
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,080
You're my biggest investor.

133
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:26,200
Of course I'll support
whatever you want to do.

134
00:05:30,110 --> 00:05:31,000
Keep an eye on the shop.

135
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:31,980
I'm going to buy groceries.

136
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:34,000
I'm still counting on it
to make me financially independent

137
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,100
and rise to great success.

138
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:38,360
Hello.

139
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:39,040
Advocate Jiang.

140
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,080
Thank you, Advocate Jiang.

141
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:42,080
You're welcome.

142
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:42,960
Advocate Jiang.

143
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:43,750
Thank you, Advocate Jiang.

144
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:44,720
Good day!

145
00:05:44,730 --> 00:05:45,820
- Advocate Jiang!
- Advocate Jiang!

146
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:46,480
Advocate Jiang.

147
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:48,400
If you hadn't stood up for us,

148
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:50,960
I wouldn't have a livelihood now.

149
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,600
It was nothing. No need to thank me.

150
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:53,560
Here.

151
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,320
Take

152
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,240
this chicken.

153
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:56,840
It's a token of gratitude
from my whole family.

154
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:58,040
Oh, I couldn't possibly.

155
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:59,360
No, you have to take it.

156
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:00,520
Here.

157
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:00,920
Take it.

158
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:02,400
All right.

159
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:03,160
Thank you.

160
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,180
Take care, Advocate Jiang.

161
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:05,800
Advocate Jiang.

162
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:06,440
Good day.

163
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:07,800
Advocate Jiang.

164
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:09,720
You...

165
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:11,390
I'm here to buy some groceries.

166
00:06:12,120 --> 00:06:13,120
Of course.

167
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:15,200
Don't worry about
the vegetables or anything else.

168
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,080
I'll get them for you.

169
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,080
Miss.

170
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,120
It's you.

171
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:35,600
Miss, your family

172
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:36,680
must be quite a large one.

173
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:39,040
What are you talking about?

174
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:41,120
I've always been grateful

175
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,560
for your help last time.

176
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:44,200
I wanted to thank you in person,

177
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:45,840
but I didn't know where you lived.

178
00:06:46,360 --> 00:06:46,880
Today,

179
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,560
Heaven has truly been kind

180
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,080
to let me meet you again.

181
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:50,920
Please

182
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,040
accept my bow of gratitude.

183
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:54,040
There's no need.

184
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:54,960
It was nothing.

185
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,600
When you see injustice, speak up.

186
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,990
When it's time to act, take action.

187
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,840
If there's anything you need,

188
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:02,040
just let me know.

189
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:03,680
Anything I need?

190
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:05,000
I'll grant you

191
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:06,000
three wishes.

192
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:07,320
No matter when

193
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:08,320
or what it is,

194
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:09,400
just say the word,

195
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:10,680
and I'll make it happen.

196
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:12,320
Aladdin's genie.

197
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:13,960
All right.

198
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,640
I'll use one of them today.

199
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:30,260
(Guaranteed Win Legal House)
This is my place.

200
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:36,600
I still don't know your name.

201
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:37,880
Jiang Xiaobai.

202
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:39,360
Jiang Xiaobai.

203
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:42,320
A little boat drifts by the river
in the evening glow,

204
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:43,720
its white sail billowing

205
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,000
as it rides the wind.

206
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,360
What a lovely name.

207
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,720
Quite the scholar, aren't you?

208
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:49,680
You flatter me.

209
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:50,840
And you?

210
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:51,480
Me?

211
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,000
My name is Sizhou.

212
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,560
That's a nice name too.

213
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:55,800
Well,

214
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:56,960
I'll be going now.

215
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,240
Bye.

216
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:00,400
Farewell.

217
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:09,240
Don't forget
you still owe me two wishes.

218
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:10,880
I won't forget.

219
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:23,480
Xiaobai,

220
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:25,680
who were you talking to?

221
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,360
Aladdin's genie.

222
00:08:29,110 --> 00:08:30,080
You wouldn't understand.

223
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,320
Goodness!

224
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:35,800
You bought so many vegetables.

225
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:37,350
How long will it
take us to eat all this?

226
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,560
These aren't vegetables.

227
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:40,000
They're my legal fees.

228
00:08:42,760 --> 00:08:43,440
My Lord,

229
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:45,390
everything is ready for
the Imperial Retreat's completion ceremony.

230
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:46,120
Once the auspicious hour arrives,

231
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:46,840
we can begin.

232
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:47,640
Good.

233
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:48,630
My Lord.

234
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,280
What happened to your hand?

235
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:51,880
I suddenly felt like

236
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:53,440
trying to tame a wild horse

237
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,640
and accidentally fell off.

238
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:55,440
Perhaps

239
00:08:55,450 --> 00:08:57,480
I was too excited about
the Imperial Retreat's completion.

240
00:08:58,490 --> 00:08:59,830
Has the Imperial Physician examined you?

241
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:00,240
Yes.

242
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,200
It's nothing serious.

243
00:09:01,520 --> 00:09:02,960
A few days of rest will do.

244
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:03,760
Then...

245
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,840
what about the lighting ceremony later?

246
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,680
I've been worried about that too.

247
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:12,840
But this arm

248
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,560
simply won't move.

249
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:16,360
My Lord.

250
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:17,720
If you trust me,

251
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,490
I'd be willing
to perform it in your place.

252
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:21,880
Excellent.

253
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:24,040
The First Prince, Sizhou, has arrived.

254
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:25,880
First Prince?

255
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:00,990
What are you laughing at?

256
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,110
Nothing.

257
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:07,600
How about going out
with me for a change of scenery?

258
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:09,280
I'm in no mood for that.

259
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:11,080
I haven't made a single profitable deal.

260
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,830
Pay no heed to the sound
of rain beating through the leaves.

261
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,920
Why not stroll on, chanting at ease?

262
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,360
What does that mean?

263
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:19,200
It means what is meant
to come will come.

264
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,480
There's no need to worry.

265
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:21,920
Besides, you have me.

266
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,080
All right.

267
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,160
I'll listen to you.

268
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,880
Where are you taking me, then?

269
00:10:26,110 --> 00:10:27,200
The Yushan Imperial Retreat.

270
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:28,240
Its completion ceremony.

271
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:29,360
Interested?

272
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:30,440
The Yushan Imperial Retreat?

273
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:34,040
Won't it be full of tall,
rich, handsome men?

274
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:35,720
So, are you coming?

275
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:36,600
Of course.

276
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,640
Maybe I'll meet my Mr. Right.

277
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,200
Official Dong, after you.

278
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,320
After you.

279
00:10:42,330 --> 00:10:43,640
Official Li, it's been a while.

280
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:44,920
It's been a long time.

281
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:45,840
It's been a long time.

282
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:49,560
- Your Highness.
- Your Highness.

283
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:52,880
Let's go.

284
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:54,120
It's been a long time.

285
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:57,440
Official Zhao, please come in.

286
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:57,880
After you.

287
00:10:58,360 --> 00:10:59,880
Are all these people officials?

288
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:00,640
Yes.

289
00:11:00,760 --> 00:11:01,400
They're

290
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:03,160
His Majesty's senior officials.

291
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:03,640
That man

292
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:05,560
is Official Shi,
Vice Minister of Revenue.

293
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:06,440
And that man

294
00:11:06,450 --> 00:11:07,760
is Official Li, Vice Minister of Works.

295
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:09,400
Vice Minister?

296
00:11:09,410 --> 00:11:10,400
Is that a high-ranking position?

297
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:12,400
You could say that.

298
00:11:12,590 --> 00:11:14,560
Is it higher than
your uncle Prince Luan's rank?

299
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:15,960
No, it isn't.

300
00:11:16,920 --> 00:11:18,040
That's a relief.

301
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:19,960
Why?

302
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:20,800
Nothing.

303
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:22,580
I'm just trying
to get a sense of the ranks.

304
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:22,920
Come on.

305
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,120
I'll show you around inside.

306
00:11:24,380 --> 00:11:24,840
All right.

307
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,680
This really is remarkable.

308
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:33,560
What material could be so transparent?

309
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:35,800
I heard it's called glass.

310
00:11:35,810 --> 00:11:36,990
It comes from Langjing Kingdom.

311
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,800
Prince Luan went to great lengths

312
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,320
to find this material.

313
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:41,640
It took considerable effort.

314
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,080
Prince Luan has truly been thoughtful.

315
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,920
His Majesty will surely be delighted

316
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:46,600
to see such a marvelous sight.

317
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:48,560
The auspicious hour has arrived.

318
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:51,040
Guests, please take your seats.

319
00:11:51,890 --> 00:11:52,200
Come on.

320
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:52,960
Sit with me.

321
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:53,800
All right.

322
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:57,880
Uncle.

323
00:11:58,500 --> 00:11:59,660
You truly put a lot of effort

324
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:00,990
into building this Imperial Retreat.

325
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,480
It was simply my duty.

326
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:05,300
Since we're all
in such high spirits today,

327
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:06,680
my dear nephew,

328
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,640
you must stay

329
00:12:07,650 --> 00:12:08,660
and have a few more drinks.

330
00:12:11,710 --> 00:12:12,560
Glad you came, right?

331
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:13,920
See any tall, rich,
handsome men you like?

332
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:14,640
(Why is she here?)

333
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,680
Why did you stop?

334
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:23,560
I just remembered

335
00:12:23,570 --> 00:12:25,000
I have important business
to attend to today.

336
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:25,880
I'll

337
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,280
visit another day.

338
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:28,880
Very well.

339
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:31,120
Since you have
important matters to attend to,

340
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,360
I won't keep you.

341
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,280
Officials of the court,

342
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:56,920
honored guests,

343
00:12:57,920 --> 00:12:58,600
today,

344
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:00,000
the Yushan Imperial Retreat

345
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,200
is finally complete.

346
00:13:01,210 --> 00:13:02,080
This is truly the result

347
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,080
of Heaven's favor

348
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:04,160
and human endeavor

349
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,600
working in harmony.

350
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:07,160
On behalf

351
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:08,560
of His Majesty,

352
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:09,800
I thank you all.

353
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,120
Empress Jingshu

354
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,480
mindful of everyone's hard work,

355
00:13:13,010 --> 00:13:14,880
specially instructed me
to prepare this banquet

356
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,520
so that we may

357
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:18,440
enjoy each other's company

358
00:13:18,450 --> 00:13:20,080
and celebrate
this joyous occasion together.

359
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:21,360
Light the lamps.

360
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:26,480
Begin the lighting ceremony.

361
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:52,120
It's beautiful.

362
00:14:10,470 --> 00:14:13,070
♪The candle burns down
to its final glow♪

363
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:16,420
♪Cold fragrance clings to my hem♪

364
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:18,820
♪You gently smooth my hair♪

365
00:14:18,820 --> 00:14:21,740
♪Yet your gaze drifts far away♪

366
00:14:24,190 --> 00:14:26,610
♪A hidden blade lies beneath your smile♪

367
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:30,290
♪You turn away
as if nothing has changed♪

368
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:32,460
♪Step by step, I walk away♪

369
00:14:32,630 --> 00:14:35,960
♪Each step breaks my heart anew♪

370
00:14:38,700 --> 00:14:41,570
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

371
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:45,180
♪Why leave me
standing alone in the wind?♪

372
00:14:45,620 --> 00:14:48,240
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

373
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:52,270
♪Yet all that's left
is warmth upon my fingertips♪

374
00:14:52,510 --> 00:14:55,560
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

375
00:14:55,930 --> 00:14:58,610
♪And write of every meeting
and every parting♪

376
00:14:58,610 --> 00:15:01,360
♪If next life asks
about the days gone by♪

377
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:04,580
♪I'll only say that once♪

378
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:06,820
♪I called your name♪

379
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:13,650
♪The silent stars hang low♪

380
00:15:15,070 --> 00:15:17,280
♪The river keeps flowing east♪

381
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:20,410
♪I linger in the old tower♪

382
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:24,190
♪Waiting for you,
though all is now empty♪

383
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:27,960
♪This life still owes us a bow♪

384
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,620
♪May the next repay us with a dream♪

385
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:34,630
♪Beyond here lie
endless mountains and rivers♪

386
00:15:34,630 --> 00:15:40,870
♪I dare not turn for one last look♪

387
00:15:41,130 --> 00:15:44,010
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

388
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:48,110
♪Why bury this heart beneath the frost?♪

389
00:15:48,110 --> 00:15:50,750
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

390
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:55,040
♪Now only fading warmth
remains in my palm♪

391
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:57,950
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

392
00:15:58,380 --> 00:16:01,100
♪And paint a winter between your brows♪

393
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:03,770
♪If we meet again in another life♪

394
00:16:04,090 --> 00:16:06,820
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

395
00:16:07,510 --> 00:16:09,800
♪Was when we first met?♪

396
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:13,460
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

397
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:16,350
♪Was when we met for the last time?♪
